# graphify input scoping (local tool config, not a build input).
#
# Scope the graph to exactly: crates/, ui/src/, scripts/, .github/workflows/,
# README.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/{BRIEF,AMENDMENTS,HANDOFF}.md. Everything else at
# the repo root (assets/, packaging/, Cargo.*, LICENSE, rust-toolchain.toml,
# ui's own package files, test.wav, etc.) is left out, not because it's
# sensitive, but because it isn't part of what was asked for.
#
# Standard gitignore semantics: a directory must be un-ignored before its
# contents can be, so each included path is un-ignored one level at a time.

# Ignore everything at the repo root by default.
/*

# Rust workspace sources.
!/crates/
!/crates/**

# Build/CI scripts (includes scripts/quant/ - the reproducible measurement
# code, not the /quant/ working directory of private dictations, which stays
# ignored below).
!/scripts/
!/scripts/**

# CI workflow definitions. .github/ only contains workflows/, so this is
# equivalent to including all of .github/.
!/.github/
!/.github/**

# Top-level docs.
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# Working notes (excluded from git by the root .gitignore, but wanted here).
!/docs/
!/docs/**

# Svelte UI: only the source, not node_modules/dist/config/lockfiles.
!/ui/
/ui/*
!/ui/src/
!/ui/src/**

# Hard excludes, kept explicit even though most are already covered by the
# allowlist above or by graphify's built-in noise-dir skips. quant/ and
# recordings*/ hold the owner's private dictations and must never be read.
/target/
/quant/
/recordings/
/recordings-pl/
/cue-audition/
/.tools/
/models/
*.wav
*.gguf
*.bin
*.jsonl
*.db
*.log

# Tauri-generated permission schemas: thousands of JSON keys, no knowledge in them.
/crates/lathe/gen/
